// A Go workspace binds the canonical component modules together during development and in
// CI. Each directory below is a separate module so that it has exactly one build
// definition, one artifact identity, and one rollback procedure, as required by
// docs/02_POLYGLOT_ENGINEERING_STANDARD.md section 8.
//
// The workspace is a development convenience, not a release mechanism. Release builds are
// produced from pinned commits and immutable artifact digests (docs/02 section 10).
//
// Toolchain versions are pinned exactly. CI must fail on toolchain drift or an unpinned
// dependency (docs/00_README.md, toolchain lifecycle).

go 1.26.8

use (
	./adapters/venues
	./components/oms
	./components/reconciliation
	./components/risk-engine
	./contracts/go
	./services/control-plane
)
